MCTAL probe: one ray through void slabs and a lattice
c Every history is the same 14 MeV neutron flying along +x from
c (-100, 0.3, 0.7) through void, so every tally is exact and hand
c computable: F4 = chord / volume, F1 = 1 per surface crossed, F2 =
c 1 / (cos * area). Slabs 1-4 are 20 cm thick (x from -40 to 40) and
c 20 x 20 cm across; slab 3 is filled with a 4 x 1 x 1 lattice of 5 cm
c elements, each holding a 3 x 10 x 10 box (cell 8, x from 1 to 4 in the
c element) in cell 9; elements -1 and 4 are filled too, only so that the
c ray entering on an element boundary finds an element. Regenerate with:
c mcnp6 i=probe.mcnp n=probe.
1 0  10 -11 15 -16 17 -18 imp:n=1
2 0  11 -12 15 -16 17 -18 imp:n=1
3 0  12 -13 15 -16 17 -18 imp:n=1 fill=1
4 0  13 -14 15 -16 17 -18 imp:n=1
5 0  -99 #1 #2 #3 #4 imp:n=1
6 0  99 imp:n=0
7 0  -22 21 -24 23 -26 25 imp:n=1 u=1 lat=1 fill=-1:4 0:0 0:0 2 5r
8 0  30 -31 32 -33 34 -35 imp:n=1 u=2
9 0  #8 imp:n=1 u=2

10 PX -40
11 PX -20
12 PX 0
13 PX 20
14 PX 40
15 PY -10
16 PY 10
17 PZ -10
18 PZ 10
21 PX 0
22 PX 5
23 PY -10
24 PY 10
25 PZ -10
26 PZ 10
30 PX 1
31 PX 4
32 PY -5
33 PY 5
34 PZ -5
35 PZ 5
40 PY 0
99 SO 200

MODE N
SDEF POS=-100 0.3 0.7 VEC=1 0 0 DIR=1 ERG=14 TME=0
NPS 100
PRDMP 2j 1
VOL 8000 8000 8000 8000 1 1 2000 300 1700
c --- plain cell list
FC4 plain cells
F4:N 1 2 3 4
c --- groups and the T bin
FC14 groups and total
F14:N (1 2) (3 4) 1 T
c --- lattice and universe levels
FC24 levels
F24:N 8 9 (8 < 7[0:3 0:0 0:0] < 3)
FC34 more levels
F34:N (8 < 7[0:1 0:0 0:0] < 3) (8 9 < 7[2 0 0] < 3)
FC44 more levels
F44:N (8 9 < 3) (8 < 7[1 0 0] 7[3 0 0] < 3) (8 < 3) T
c --- multipliers, three-digit exponents
FC54 multipliers
F54:N 1 2
FM54 (1) (2) (1e-110)
c --- energy and time bins with totals; no total; cumulative
FC64 energy and time
F64:N 1 2 3 4
E64 1 10 20
T64 100 1e5
FC74 energy without total
F74:N 1 2
E74 1 10 20 NT
FC84 cumulative energy
F84:N 1 2
E84 1 10 20 C
c --- user bins
FC94 user bins from FT INC
F94:N 1 2
FT94 INC
FU94 0 1 T
c --- surface current with cosine bins and segments; surface flux
FC1 current, cosine bins
F1:N 11 12
C1 0 1 T
FC11 current, segments
F11:N 11 12
FS11 -40
FC2 surface flux
F2:N 11 12
SD2 400 400
